state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"C001053","fullName":"Rep. Cole, Tom [R-OK-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OK"},{"bioguideId":"L000597","fullName":"Rep. Lee, Laurel M. [R-FL-15]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-08","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"B001322","fullName":"Rep. Baumgartner, Michael [R-WA-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-08","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T21:24:12+00:00","id":"hr3453-119","introducedDate":"2025-05-15","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-01-13","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 379."},"laws":[],"number":"3453","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Education","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"L000595","district":5,"fullName":"Rep. Letlow, Julia [R-LA-5]","party":"R","state":"LA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2026-01-13","actionDesc":"Reported to House","text":"<p><strong>Empower Charter School Educators to Lead Act</strong></p><p>This bill makes changes to the Charter Schools Program (CSP), which authorizes competitive grants to state entities (e.g., state educational agencies and state charter school boards) to&nbsp;support high-quality charter schools.&nbsp;</p><p>Specifically, the bill allows state entities to use up to 5% of their CSP grant funds to make pre-charter planning subgrants to certain prospective charter applicants.</p><p>The bill specifies that state entities may also (1)&nbsp;fund a revolving loan fund or similar mechanisms for the expenses of eligible applicants prior to receiving CSP subgrants,&nbsp;and (2)&nbsp;provide assistance to eligible applicants in locating and accessing a charter school facility.</p><p>Under the current CSP, state entities must use at least 7% of their CSP grant funds to provide technical assistance to eligible applicants and authorized public chartering agencies. The bill instead allows state entities to use not more than 10% of these funds for technical assistance.</p>","updateDate":"2026-04-01T18:37:05Z","versionCode":"07"}],"title":"Empower Charter School Educators to Lead Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-23T23:06:24Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-23T23:06:24Z"}
